;;; A bare `_` as an `is-a` subject is dropped at load, in silence —
;;; **W29**, regression `is-a-arg` (`corpus/regressions.toml`),
;;; under Q-M1e2.22.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two kernel `is-a` facts, the second writing the bare `_` as its subject.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing (Q-M1e2.22), so the program is
;;; refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command that reads it
;;; exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what it answers ──────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `ec004a48` (the engine `916d97ac`'s), release and debug alike: the
;;; loader dropped the `_` and stored the one-argument `(is-a T)`, with no
;;; line. H was empty and R {∅}, exit 0, and `--dump-answer`'s state file
;;; listed `(is-a T)`. Today the parse refuses the `_`.

(is-a a T)
(is-a _ T)
